<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46828" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλέμᾰτος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		 and 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέματος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>idle,
			vain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				15.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				23.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ τᾶς ἀλεμάτω ψυχᾶς</span>
			prob. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.4
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδεμ-, ἀδαμ-</span> codd.); of a
			person, Timo <i><span class="en">
				34.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				66.4
			</span></i> (cj.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βροντή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sotad.
					2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρὸς ἑκηβολία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.75
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαντασίη</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				11.350
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>
			<i>idly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1206
			</span></i>; <i>in vain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Cer.</u>
				91
			</span></i>: so neut. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλέματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					4.590
				</span></i>
			.</div>
